   "t": 1791258677.311541,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "I've stopped cleanly on my pre-declared rule, with final specification [feature 25+, feature 4+] at in-sample Sharpe 1.4020. This was a disciplined, fully replayable search: init \u2192 extend_best \u2192 stop, with the stopping rule declared *before* seeing any results.\n\nNow let me think about the out-of-sample prediction. In-sample Sharpe of 1.40 from a 2-feature combination found via only two moves (not an extensive search with many trials) is a good sign for replayability \u2014 minimal data-mining relative to the 80-candidate universe. However, there's still some optimism bias:\n- `init` picked the best of 80 candidates (some in-sample selection bias)\n- `extend_best` picked the best-improving second feature\n- Costs are already netted in, which is good \u2014 this isn't a gross Sharpe illusion\n\nTypical IS-to-OOS Sharpe degradation for simple, low-complexity specs (2 features, equal weight, no further overfitting) is often a shrinkage of 30-50%. I'll predict conservatively."
